## User Access

The discovered credentials (`admin` / `thisisagoodpassword`) did not correspond to any system account directly, but were tested against the one real user found in `/etc/passwd`: **`john`**.

```bash
ssh john@10.129.47.59
# password: thisisagoodpassword
```

This succeeded — the admin panel's password had been reused for the `john` system account.

```
john@base:~$ cat user.txt
f54846c258f3b4612f78a819573d158e
```

